# Optional runtime settings for `docker compose`. Copy to .env.docker (gitignored) and
# uncomment what you need, then `docker compose up -d` again. Without .env.docker,
# investigations use the mock provider: no key, no network.
# The key is read when the container starts; it is never part of an image.
# Note: anyone who can run `docker inspect` on this machine can read container variables.

# GroqCloud (check its terms and limits first, ADR 0015):
# SENTINEL_LLM_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# SENTINEL_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# SENTINEL_LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# SENTINEL_LLM_API_KEY=

# Ollama running on this machine (not in a container): the container reaches the host as
# host.docker.internal (Docker Desktop), not localhost.
# SENTINEL_LLM_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# SENTINEL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# SENTINEL_LLM_MODEL=<model you pulled>

# SENTINEL_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
# SENTINEL_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=1500
